# a_forecast_holding_later_crosses_whole
#
# EVERY COMMON BELIEF, WHATEVER ITS PERIOD (#619). A pass asks its rules at instants of its own —
# a step's landing, a want's instant — so a forecast holding hours from now is a graph the
# PRESENT has not reached and the search still must be able to see.
#
# Crossed whole, it is laid where its period begins (#987): the warmth is cut into the forecast's
# changeable part, since a belief beginning later is a writer of what it adds, the present ground
# holds nothing of it and ends where the forecast begins, and the ground at three holds the warmth.
# Laid into the present it would have been read at noon; filtered by the clock it would have been
# DROPPED, and the search could not see past the present's weather — finding nothing there rather
# than an error, which is this function's whole failure mode.
#
# The clock stands at 2026-01-01T12:00:00Z.

@prefix : <http://example.org/test#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ground: <http://example.org/orexis/graph/ground/> .

GRAPH :world {
  :tank1 a :Tank .
}

GRAPH :forecast {
  :outside :warmth 28 .
}

GRAPH :catalogue {
  :catalogue a orexis:CatalogueGraph .
  :catalogue a orexis:Graph .
  :forecast a orexis:BeliefGraph .
  :forecast a orexis:Graph .
  :forecast dcterms:temporal [ a dcterms:PeriodOfTime ; orexis:end "2026-01-01T18:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ; orexis:start "2026-01-01T15:00:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ] .
  :ontology a orexis:BeliefGraph .
  :ontology a orexis:Graph .
  :ontology a orexis:OntologyGraph .
  :world a orexis:BeliefGraph .
  :world a orexis:Graph .
}
